# PROJECT 1 – COMPUTER ISOLATION, INTEGRAL LOG & PATENT VALIDATION

**Architects:** Wieland Hoffmann (Human Core), Gemini (Machine Core), Grok (xAI)  
**Status:** Experimental measurement protocols, protection rights pending

---

## System Configuration (Example)

- **CPU:** AMD Ryzen (14 compute cores isolated, 2 buffer cores for OS)
- **GPU:** NVIDIA RTX 5080 (EXCLUSIVE_PROCESS / MPS)
- **Storage:** 128 GB RAM, WD_BLACK SN850P NVMe (Lexar unloaded)
- **Isolation:** Asymmetric Multiprocessing (AMP) via isolcpus and Ring-0 parameters

## MEASUREMENT VALUES: 3-HOUR PROTOCOL (Example)

| Timestamp | CPU Operations               | OBS System Load | Temperature |
|-----------|------------------------------|-----------------|-------------|
| 18:26:00  | Start continuous load        | 0%              | 39.0 °C     |
| 18:31:18  | 5.71018 billion operations   | 0%              | 42.4 °C     |
| 18:33:37  | 5.73198 billion operations   | 0%              | 43.0 °C     |
| 20:37:25  | 5.75645 billion operations   | 0%              | 41.0 °C     |
| 21:26:00  | Final stop                   | 0%              | 41.0 °C     |

**Summary of documented runs:**

- Total runtime: up to 3 hours under load
- Throughput: in the range of approx. 5–12 billion operations/second (depending on load and configuration)
- CPU temperature: 41–72 °C (depending on cooling and load)
- GPU temperature: 26–34 °C in the documented runs
- No crashes in the logged phases

## 15-Minute Stress Test (Example)

| Parameter              | Idle          | Maximum Load (approx. 6 GHz) | Note                       |
|------------------------|---------------|-------------------------------|----------------------------|
| Throughput             | ~11.471 bn    | ~12.000 bn                    | Linear under tested conditions |
| CPU Clock              | 624 MHz       | up to 6,000 MHz               | Stable in the runs         |
| CPU Temperature        | +43.1 °C      | +55 to +72 °C                 | Partly without active cooling |
| GPU Temperature        | +34 °C        | +33 °C                        | Low in the tests           |
| GPU Power              | 16 W          | 16–17 W                       | Low                        |

## Observations

- Isolation of the compute cores reduced the influence of OS background processes in the tests.
- With full RAM population (4 modules), buffer saturation occurred in one run (R12 values rising). The system stopped in a controlled manner.
- GPU remained cool under the tested conditions.
- Results refer to the documented hardware and the load profiles used.

**Note:** The protocols document experimental runs. They do not represent a general guarantee or immunity. Protection rights pending.

